l/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md Sections 5.4, 10.5-10.6, 13.12 and 13.13.\n2|\n3|Verify with your own instruments: (1) Whole-Story diff — story_final: the candidate tree against trunk e4e3e8834675cf3814effd3b2673b4931dfbf311 is the complete Story delta (replayed checkpoints 8a757e0 14yo67 and bde093e 3k3e6m plus this leaf); confirm both replayed checkpoints are signed and their trees equal the originally accepted trees (d805720 and 8bcc13f) except LOGBOOK.md whose two replay resolutions kept every entry newest-first (trunk's 3lt2xv entry preserved); enumerate every changed path of the Story; task-board.config.json byte-identical to trunk; this leaf touched only its stated paths (README, LOGBOOK, four traceability files, the new internal/crashgate package) beyond the checkpoints — no sessckpt/matjournal source change. (2) Registry derivation — the 94 boundary IDs must be parsed from the pinned Section 13.13 table by the derivation test with zero hand-typed IDs: extract the table yourself and diff the ID set and the per-family ranges; plant a renamed ID in a private copy of the document and confirm the derivation test reddens; audit the classification of every ID into driven (31 IDs / 48 paths) versus NOT APPLICABLE (63 IDs / 121 paths): for each NOT APPLICABLE path the named owner must be an unlanded owner per the pinned text and the landed code (spot-check at least ten: a row whose durable fact IS a checkpoint capture or journal transition but was marked N/A is a finding). (3) Conformance records — for every driven path rerun the producer's row and read its JSON record: boundary ID, path, operation IDs, pre/post durable facts, external effect and status probe, winning lease before/after, native identity/binding before/after, selected outcome and evidence must all be present and consistent with the crash actually injected (compare the record against the on-disk state you observe after replaying the row); rerun the two real-SIGKILL rows twice; then inject your own crashes at