er boundary written under .temp during the run and attached in the evidence tarball, narrowing mutants for the evaluator's classification predicates and every rejection rule with an applied harmless SURVIVED control, and a conformance matrix mapping each 13.12/13.13 clause and each boundary ID to a test row, a NOT APPLICABLE row with owner, or a stated bound. No product behavior change is expected; if a boundary exposes a defect in sessckpt/matjournal, fix it minimally in this leaf with a RED-first regression and say so. This is the FINAL leaf (story_final CR): carry the Story-close items — the traceability registry bindings for 13.12/13.13 (currently 13.12 unmeasured) updated to the real conformance harness with honest coverage text and acceptance cases, reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256 re-pinned; README package sections (sessckpt and matjournal exist; add yours) with test commands and no capability claim; LOGBOOK entry. Managed Story worktree contract: .temp/STORY-260830-2rqigd/worktree on branch task-board/story/STORY-260830-2rqigd whose tip is the 3k3e6m checkpoint; leave the candidate UNCOMMITTED, never commit on the Story branch, never edit .task-board directly, never self-accept; if origin/main moves before your handoff (it will: a release-agnostic validation command is landing on trunk), run task-board worktree refresh-candidate TASK-260830-17ootk and restore any trunk-changed path the refresh left stale with a single-path git checkout HEAD -- <path> (task-board.config.json in particular must equal HEAD); before handoff verify git status shows only candidate paths (no __pycache__, no .pyc). Evidence contract as in the repository DoD. Read the Curator-managed go-testing-tools skill first; all CI local; run the full configured validation suite once before the handoff; hand off no later than 3.5 hours in (a 13-point leaf: if the full registry cannot be finished, hand off a reviewable slice with the remaining boundaries enumerated precisely — but the Story-close