partial file, a receipt without a blob) and assert exactly one outcome with fail-closed parking on contradictory evidence. (4) Exclusivity and rejections — attack the evaluator: construct evidence satisfying both safe_retry and explicit_rollback predicates and confirm recoverable_parked_state; construct the ten rejection cases yourself (two live authorities, unfenced continuation, new-session launch, fresh handle, blank relabel, different realm, moved lease) and confirm none is reported as a successful outcome and each parks with durable blocking evidence and a frozen phase; confirm no fourth outcome string exists anywhere (grep the package and the records). (5) Section 13.12 — the seven driven rows reproduced; for the twelve rows naming unlanded owners confirm the owner is genuinely unlanded. (6) Mutation — rerun mutant_harness.py in an isolated copy (9 KILLED + control), rerun each KILLED twice, plant at least four narrowing mutants of your own on classification predicates the producer did not mutate (exhaustiveness fallback removed for one family; exclusivity check skipped when evidence lists are empty; a rejection case admitted as safe_retry when the lease tuple matches; N/A rows counted as driven) plus an applied harmless SURVIVED control; per-plant raw logs, subprocess exits, precise denominators. (7) Story-close items — registry: section:13.13 partial 9/11 with the 13.13#4/#5 journal-halves gap disclosed, section:13.12 unmeasured with the harness case (judge whether \"unmeasured\" is honest given seven driven rows — a measured partial may be the truthful binding), 2 new acceptance cases, reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256 re-pinned to a1b48479…: recompute the projection digest independently, confirm every claimed clause line exists and each binding names an existing production declaration driven by an acceptance case (plant a self-minted claim — refused), tracecheck 26/489 and 107 cases reproduced; README package sections (sessckpt, matjournal, crashgate) with 