{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cd77","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae83-44da-79a0-be6d-cdb96bee744a"},"sequence":1302,"recorded_at":1780531400002599,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"43909339-e6a4-48a8-9111-b9f3b1e533e8","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"43909339-e6a4-48a8-9111-b9f3b1e533e8","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"43909339-e6a4-48a8-9111-b9f3b1e533e8"},"call_id":"call_01a0ae87aad6778f8adbb3cd66875563","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-2rqigd/worktree/internal/crashgate/doc.go`.\n1|// Package crashgate executes the Section 13.13 crash/restart outcome gate\n2|// over the landed checkpoint and journal owners\n3|// (STORY-260830-2rqigd, TASK-260830-17ootk).\n4|//\n5|// Authority: relux-works/agent-session-manager-spec@v0.6.0, Section\n6|// 13.13 (crash/restart outcome gate) and Section 13.12 (failure\n7|// matrix). The task scope cites the same section numbers of v0.5.0;\n8|// the headings are retained in v0.6.0.\n9|//\n10|// The package owns the boundary registry: every crash boundary ID of\n11|// the Section 13.13 registry table plus the CR-CLONE prose range,\n12|// each classified per direct/task-board path as reachable through\n13|// the landed owners or NOT APPLICABLE with the exact owning\n14|// flow/package named. The enumeration is verified against the pinned\n15|// specification by a derivation test (no hand-typed boundary list);\n16|// the classification is explicit harness data, reviewed with the\n17|// conformance matrix in TRACEABILITY.md.\n18|//\n19|// The package owns no recovery behavior and changes none. Every\n20|// reachable row is driven through the landed production entries:\n21|//\n22|//   - internal/sessckpt Store.Capture for checkpoint-capture\n23|//     boundaries (blob-then-receipt install, receipt replay);\n24|//     recovery is the idempotent retry converging on the recorded\n25|//     result (safe_retry by construction; capture is append-only\n26|//     and has no rollback or parked semantics).\n27|//   - internal/matjournal Store.Create and its journal updates for\n28|//     journal boundaries, with Store.Recover as the recovery\n29|//     evaluator classifying exactly one of safe_retry,\n30|//     explicit_rollback, or recoverable_parked_state.\n31|//\n32|// Reused owners: internal/sessrepo (chain reads, checkpoint\n33|// attestation), internal/secconftest (crash-injection vocabulary),\n34|// internal/specdoc (pinned text; test binaries only), and the\n35|// scalar/canonical/axerror grammar owners. Product code never reads\n36|// the specification text.\n37|//\n38|// Stated bounds: boundaries whose durable write belongs to an\n39|// unlanded owner (lease arbitration beyond sessrepo persistence,\n40|// terminal creation, provider process start and native discovery,\n41|// bridge launch/export/adopt execution, sync transfer, lifecycle\n42|// orchestration, the clone flow) are recorded NOT APPLICABLE, never\n43|// silently skipped. Status probes stay modeled inputs, as in\n44|// matjournal. The package adds no ax command, no doctor result, and\n45|// no runtime capability claim.\n46|package crashgate","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
