owned by sync, lease, provider, bridge, and lifecycle flows (SSH disconnect, quarantine, divergence, quiesce failure, plugin crash, missing bridge, concurrent takeovers, stale owner, corrupt index) belong to their unlanded owners.\\\"\\n}\\n---\\n{\\n \\\"kind\\\": \\\"section_binding\\\",\\n \\\"keys\\\": [\\n  \\\"section:13.13\\\"\\n ],\\n \\\"production\\\": {\\n  \\\"path\\\": \\\"internal/matjournal/recover.go\\\",\\n  \\\"declaration\\\": \\\"Recover\\\"\\n },\\n \\\"acceptance_cases\\\": [\\n  \\\"materialization-journal-recovery\\\",\\n  \\\"crash-gate-journal-conformance\\\",\\n  \\\"crash-gate-checkpoint-conformance\\\"\\n ],\\n \\\"coverage\\\": \\\"partial\\\",\\n \\\"gap\\\": \\\"Recover with the crashgate conformance harness discharges 9 of the 11 normative clauses of Section 13.13 (every-boundary injection for checkpoint/journal-observable paths, exactly-one classification, safe_retry meaning, ambiguity rule, no fourth outcome, conformance record contents, two-live-authority and substitution rejection, unfenced-continuation parking); clauses 13.13#4 and 13.13#5 are discharged only for their journal-durable halves because rollback/parked visibility through event, CLI/status, audit, and lifecycle-projection surfaces belongs to unlanded owners, and boundaries owned by lease, terminal, provider, bridge, sync, lifecycle, and clone flows are recorded NOT APPLICABLE with owners rather than injected.\\\",\\n \\\"clauses\\\": [\\n  {\\n   \\\"id\\\": \\\"13.13#1\\\",\\n   \\\"line\\\": 9969,\\n   \\\"excerpt\\\": \\\"Every implementation MUST inject a crash and a clean process restart at every\\\",\\n   \\\"acceptance_cases\\\": [\\n    \\\"crash-gate-journal-conformance\\\",\\n    \\\"crash-gate-checkpoint-conformance\\\"\\n   ]\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"id\\\": \\\"13.13#2\\\",\\n   \\\"line\\\": 9971,\\n   \\\"excerpt\\\": \\\"After restart, the recovery evaluator MUST classify the operation into exactly\\\",\\n   \\\"acceptance_cases\\\": [\\n    \\\"crash-gate-journal-conformance\\\"\\n   ]\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"id\\\": \\\"13.13#3\\\",\\n   \\\"line\\\": 9976,\\n   \\\"excerpt\\\": \\\"| <code>safe_retry</code> | The same logical operation can continue or return its recorded result using every caller-stable operation/materialization/transaction/bridge ID and byte-identical immutable input. The winning lease and the exact persisted Provider Identity Record or task-board manager reference/Ax Binding are unchanged. A retry MUST reconcile an uncertain external effect before issuing it again and MUST NOT allocate another process, manager, native handle, lease epoch, staging authority, or transaction root. | The pre-crash durable receipt or journal phase, the post-restart status result for every possibly executed provider/bridge/external effect, the unchanged winning lease, the unchanged native identity/binding, and the single returned or advanced durable result. |\\\",\\n   \\\"acceptance_cases\\\": [\\n    \\\"crash-gate-journal-conformance\\\",\\n    \\\"crash-gate-checkpoint-conformance\\\"\\n   ]\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"id\\n---\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 3442,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 861,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
